# Backend (overview v3.1)

Share one domain model across mobile, MERN web app, and Next.js preview. **Score math lives on the server.** Validate with the internal reputation-engine tester before applying updates to real profiles.

## Own on the API

Auth and verification, profiles and privacy, ratings + reputation, disputes, entitlements/billing hooks, QR/NFC identity resolution.

## Invariants

- Public preview endpoints return card-safe fields only (no snapshot, no rate)
- Rating submit requires an authenticated app session and remaining **give** quota
- Persist `Sold`, `n`, `W` components; do not recompute from a naive mean
- OTP/email/push/stores are client-paid; define interfaces first

```ts
// ❌ BAD — client sends a new score
await db.profiles.update({ score: body.score })

// ✅ GOOD — client sends categories + relationship; server applies the formula
const R = mean(categories)
const Snew = Sold + alpha(n) * W * (R - Sold)
```
